cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Promethea: An open, CI-validated OpenMC benchmark of the Molten Salt Reactor Experiment"
message: "If you use Promethea in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bui"
    given-names: "Khai"
    alias: "KhaiB10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KhaiB10/promethea"
url: "https://github.com/KhaiB10/promethea"
abstract: >-
  Promethea is an open, primary-source-anchored OpenMC reproduction of
  the Molten Salt Reactor Experiment (MSRE, ORNL, 1965) criticality
  benchmark, with deterministic CI, full citation audit against
  ORNL-TM-0728/730, and machine-verifiable k-effective at multiple
  cross-section libraries. v0.4.0 extends the toolchain to the
  two-fluid Molten Salt Breeder Reactor (MSBR, ORNL-4528, 1971).
keywords:
  - "molten salt reactor"
  - "MSRE"
  - "MSBR"
  - "OpenMC"
  - "Monte Carlo"
  - "neutronics"
  - "reactor physics"
  - "criticality benchmark"
  - "reproducibility"
license: MIT
